r Arroyo, Lightner\nCreek, Animas River, First Fork Red Creek, Basin Creek, South\nFork Texas Creek, Lake Creek, Weasel Skin Creek, Deadwood Creek,\nVallecito Creek, Florida River, Beaver Creek, Junction Creek, San\nJuan Arroyo, West Fork Shearer Creek, Falls Creek, Taylor Creek,\nCastle Creek, Plata River, First Fork Piedra River, Dry Creek,\nSouth Fork Lightner Creek, Little Bear Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango, La Plata, Falfa, Hesperus, Bondad, Breen, Mayday, Kline,\nMarvel, Redmesa and Vallecito.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07d99f92410912a16ec19126592452a544313bbe.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07d99f92410912a16ec19126592452a544313bbe.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:52AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinues.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 600 AM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads\nremain closed due to flooding with road washouts also occurring.\nStreams and dry washes continue to rise due to excess runoff from\nearlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 352 AM MDT, local law enforcement reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring. Between 1.5 and 2\ninches of rain have fallen.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nDry Creek, Florida River, Little Bear Creek, Ute Creek, Spring\nCreek, Crowbar Creek, Bear Creek, Rock Creek, Hayden Creek, Salt\nCreek, Beaver Creek and Pinos River, Los.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nBayfield, Ignacio, Ox