, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is imminent or ongoing with additional rounds of showers\nand thunderstorms expected through Friday afternoon. Rivers and\ncreeks may still experience high waters even after rainfall has\nended.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e0dbcacb680ad71bb79dff518cb60ff22ebdb688.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T05:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 230552 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1152 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Several creeks, streams, and rivers have already reached flood stage due to persistent rainfall, and modeled responses suggest several others will do the same overnight. - Impacts from high water levels and flooding may be seen throughout Friday. - A few ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T06:36:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in 